  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $6?$\n\n- ${R}_{5}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5$\n- ${R}^{5}$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{6}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 6$ matrices over $R$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{5}[t])=5+1=6.\\,\u2713\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{5})=5\\ne 6.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6}(R))={6}^{2}=36\\ne 6.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
